To tell the truth (hopefully this will not be construed as a flame), I
don't think that was amazing misfortune at all.  It was player error,
something which theoretically should be avoidable--e.g. by not holding
two bags of holding, by inspecting monsters before attacking them.

After all, if player error could be avoided totally, Nethack wouldn't be
a challenge anymore, no?  I can't count the number of posts by players
discovering, to their horror, that they killed the Wiz on a water square,
and then pushed a boulder onto it; or blew up the Bell, Book, or
Candle in a bag of holding accident; or used the 'y' key when headed
northwest towards the shopkeeper or ate an elf when one is an Elf, or...

IMHO, true misfortune would be something like never finding a shop,
never getting a wish, never getting holy water, AND falling through
a trap door onto the level where you froze the Wiz with a potion,
or something along those lines. :)


